A||||3||88formula||02 voltage at  WOT?||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||10-20-2001||08:42 PM||||What should the 02 sensor voltage be at wide open throttle?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-20-2001||09:16 PM||||Whatever it feels like.... the O2 sensor will change constantly depending on exhaust O2 content even at WOT.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-20-2001||09:45 PM||||At WOT, the O2 will not switch back and forth like closed loop.<P>Generally, the O2 will be somewhere above 900mV at WOT. It might go as high as 1000mV, but generally, above 900. Below 800mV the engine is getting a bit lean at WOT.<P>The O2 is a "narrow-band" O2 so there is no way to figure out what the AFR vs voltage is, so the rule of thumb is to stay above 800mV to ensure you aren't too lean. 900mV is likely in the 12.5:1 ratio range. <P>Once you back out of the throttle and closed loop takes over, the O2 will start swinging between 0 and about 800-900mV.<P>Why do you ask?||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||10-21-2001||10:58 AM||||Thanks you very much Terry and Theogre.||||reg||1
